//? Title: Dynamic Time Warping: Actual Alignments, Costs and the Limits of Elastic Similarity
//? Subtitle: The original stretched sequence and sinusoid, exact dynamic-programming evidence and recorded GunPoint motions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given two numeric recordings, we want to compare their shapes when similar
features occur at different sample indices. A rigid comparison pairs equal
positions and can confuse timing differences with amplitude differences.
Dynamic time warping chooses a minimum-cost monotone alignment instead.
We begin with a tiny repeated-value example, inspect the actual prefix
costs and traceback, retain the original time-distorted sinusoid, and
align fixed recorded GunPoint motions through the canonical data loader.
Exact work counts, nonmetric counterexamples and checked numerical/capture
boundaries qualify what the resulting similarity does and does not mean.
)

\toc

> Align a repeated value before discussing a large waveform

Let a=[1,2,3] and b=[1,1,2,3]. The path (0,0),(0,1),(1,2),(2,3)
pairs the first value of a with both initial ones in b, then matches the
twos and threes. Every local absolute difference is zero. The following
program prints all twelve actual accumulated costs and draws the selected
path through those cells. Cell (i,j) uses zero-based observation indices
and displays D(i+1,j+1) in the prefix-length recurrence below.
The diagram uses the solver's captured values
and returned indices; it does not rerun or reconstruct the search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dtw_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1,2,3},{1,1,2,3});
  std::print("Original tiny distance {}; path pairs {}; cells {}; predecessor reads {}; capture entries {}.\n\n",t.result.distance,t.result.path_a.size(),t.work.cells,t.work.predecessor_reads,t.captured_entries);
  std::print("| a index | b index | local absolute cost | accumulated cost |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2.2;box.height=1.2;box.font_size=24;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.a.size();++i)for(std::size_t j=0;j<t.b.size();++j){
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} |\n",i,j,std::abs(t.a[i]-t.b[j]),t.cumulative[i*t.b.size()+j]);
    bool selected=false;for(std::size_t k=0;k<t.result.path_a.size();++k)selected|=t.result.path_a[k]==int(i)&&t.result.path_b[k]==int(j);
    box.fill=selected?dm::graphics::RGB{187,247,208}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
    d.node(std::format("{},{}",i,j),{2.8*j,-2.8*double(i)},std::format("({},{})\nD={:.0f}",i,j,t.cumulative[i*t.b.size()+j]),box);
  }
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke route;route.color={37,99,235};route.width=3;
  for(std::size_t k=1;k<t.result.path_a.size();++k)d.edge(std::format("{},{}",t.result.path_a[k-1],t.result.path_b[k-1]),std::format("{},{}",t.result.path_a[k],t.result.path_b[k]),"",route);
  std::print("\nChosen path:");for(std::size_t k=0;k<t.result.path_a.size();++k)std::print(" ({},{})",t.result.path_a[k],t.result.path_b[k]);std::print(".\n");
  d.text({4.2,1.6},"Actual prefix costs; selected zero-cost alignment in blue",24).save_svg("build/dtw_tiny.svg");
}
```
