> Measure the recurrence and account for storage

Every one of the n*m positive cells is evaluated, reading three
predecessor slots including infinite border slots. Traceback visits
L output pairs. The implementation uses two double cost rows and one
predecessor byte per positive cell. Ordinary calls retain no input or
cost-table history, but predecessor storage still makes total scratch
space O(n*m); this is not a linear-space traceback algorithm.

The next square-size sweep checks actual cell/read counts. It also
compares required double-buffer slots: the former full-table design
used (N+1)², while rolling rows use 2(N+1). Those slot counts follow
from buffer dimensions; they are not measured process memory. Capturing
a trace additionally retains N² accumulated doubles, N² directions and
the inputs. No panel measures execution time.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dtw_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <numbers>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double>x,cells,old_slots,new_slots;
  std::print("| N | actual cells | predecessor reads | path pairs | captured entries | old full-table double slots | rolling double slots |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{16,32,64,128,256,512}){
    const auto u=dm::seql(0,double(n-1),n)/double(n-1);
    const std::vector<double>a=dm::sin(2*std::numbers::pi*u),b=dm::sin(2*std::numbers::pi*dm::pow(u,1.6));
    const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace(a,b);
    if(t.work.cells!=n*n||t.work.predecessor_reads!=3*n*n||t.captured_entries!=2*n*n+2*n)throw std::runtime_error("work identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,t.work.cells,t.work.predecessor_reads,t.result.path_a.size(),t.captured_entries,(n+1)*(n+1),2*(n+1));
    x.push_back(std::log2(n));cells.push_back(std::log2(t.work.cells));old_slots.push_back(std::log2((n+1)*(n+1)));new_slots.push_back(std::log2(2*(n+1)));
  }
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,cells,"DP cells",{37,99,235}).points(x,cells,"",{37,99,235},5)
   .title("Actual recurrence cells: quadratic in N").x_label("log2(N)").y_label("log2(actual cells)").y_limits(0,23);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,old_slots,"former table",{220,38,38}).line(x,new_slots,"rolling rows",{37,99,235})
   .title("Double-buffer slots from dimensions").x_label("log2(N)").y_label("log2(required double slots)").y_limits(0,23);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,550).title("Work and buffer geometry are distinct from timing and total memory")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/dtw_work.svg");
}
```
